.\" DO NOT MODIFY THIS FILE!  It was generated by help2man 1.49.3.
.TH NIMBLE "1" "April 2026" "nimble 2.2.10" "User Commands"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
nimble \- Nim Package Installer
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.B nimble
[\fI\,nimbleopts\/\fR] \fI\,COMMAND \/\fR[\fI\,cmdopts\/\fR]
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.SS "Commands:"
.TP
install
[pkgname, ...]     Installs a list of packages.
[\-d, \fB\-\-depsOnly]\fR   Only install dependencies. Leave out pkgname
.IP
to install deps for a local nimble package.
.TP
[\-p, \fB\-\-passNim]\fR
Forward specified flag to compiler.
.TP
[\-\-noRebuild ]
Don't rebuild binaries if they're up\-to\-date.
.TP
develop
[pkgname, ...]     Clones a list of packages for development.
.TP
Adds them to a develop file if specified or
to `nimble.develop` if not specified and
executed in package's directory.
.TP
[\-\-withDependencies]
Puts in develop mode also the dependencies
of the packages in the list or of the current
directory package if the list is empty.
.TP
[\-p, \fB\-\-path\fR path]
Specifies the path whether the packages should
be cloned.
.TP
[\-a, \fB\-\-add\fR path]
Adds a package at given path to a specified
develop file or to `nimble.develop` if not
specified and executed in package's directory.
.TP
[\-r, \fB\-\-removePath\fR path]
Removes a package at given path from a
specified develop file or from `nimble.develop`
if not specified and executed in package's
directory.
.TP
[\-n, \fB\-\-removeName\fR name]
Removes a package with a given name from
a specified develop file or from `nimble.develop`
if not specified and executed in package's
directory.
.TP
[\-i, \fB\-\-include\fR file]
Includes a develop file into a specified
develop file or to `nimble.develop` if not
specified and executed in package's directory.
.TP
[\-e, \fB\-\-exclude\fR file]
Excludes a develop file from a specified
develop file or from `nimble.develop` if not
specified and executed in package's directory.
.TP
[\-g, \fB\-\-global]\fR
Creates an old style link file in the special
`links` directory. It is read by Nim to be
able to use global develop mode packages.
Nimble uses it as a global develop file if a
local one does not exist.
.TP
check
Verifies the validity of a package in the
current working directory.
.TP
init
[pkgname]          Initializes a new Nimble project in the
.TP
current directory or if a name is provided a
new directory of the same name.
.TP
[\-\-git, \fB\-\-hg]\fR
Creates a git/hg repo in the new nimble project.
.TP
publish
Publishes a package on nim\-lang/packages.
The current working directory needs to be the
top level directory of the Nimble package.
.TP
uninstall
[pkgname, ...]     Uninstalls a list of packages.
[\-i, \fB\-\-inclDeps]\fR   Uninstalls package and dependent package(s).
.TP
build
[opts, ...] [bin]  Builds a package. Passes options to the Nim
.IP
compiler.
.TP
clean
Clean build artifacts.
.TP
guide
Open the Nimble User Guide in your preferred browser.
.TP
add
Adds packages to your project's dependencies.
.TP
run
[opts, ...] [bin]  Builds and runs a package.
.TP
Binary needs to be specified after any
compilation options if there are several
binaries defined. Any flags after the binary
or \fB\-\-\fR arg are passed to the binary when it is run.
.TP
c, cc, js
[opts, ...] f.nim  Builds a file inside a package. Passes options
.IP
to the Nim compiler.
.TP
test
Compiles and executes tests.
.TP
[\-c, \fB\-\-continue]\fR
Don't stop execution on a failed test.
.TP
[opts, ...]
Passes options to the Nim compiler.
.TP
doc, doc2
[opts, ...] f.nim  Builds documentation for a file inside a
.IP
package. Passes options to the Nim compiler.
.TP
refresh
[url]              Refreshes the package list. A package list URL
.IP
can be optionally specified.
.TP
search
pkg/tag            Searches for a specified package. Search is
.IP
performed by tag and by name.
.IP
[\-\-ver, \fB\-\-version]\fR Queries remote server for package version.
.TP
list
Lists all packages.
.TP
[\-i, \fB\-\-installed]\fR
Lists all installed packages.
.IP
[\-\-ver, \fB\-\-version]\fR Also display versions for packages.
[\-n, \fB\-\-nimbinaries]\fR  Lists all installed packages.
.TP
tasks
Lists the tasks specified in the Nimble
package's Nimble file.
.TP
path
pkgname ...        Shows absolute path to the installed packages
.IP
specified.
.TP
dump
[pkgname]          Outputs Nimble package information for
.TP
external tools. The argument can be a
\&.nimble file, a project directory or
the name of an installed package.
.TP
[\-\-ini, \fB\-\-json]\fR
Selects the output format (the default is \fB\-\-ini\fR). Only applicable to package information.
.TP
[\-\-collect]
Collects all the packages in the dependency tree of the given package and shows the result in the console.
.TP
[\-\-solve]
Solves the dependency tree of the given package and shows the result in the console.
.TP
lock
Generates or updates a package lock file.
.TP
upgrade
[pkgname, ...]     Upgrades a list of packages in the lock file.
.TP
deps
Outputs dependencies for current package.
.TP
[\-\-tree]
Outputs dependency tree.
.TP
[\-\-inverted]
Outputs inverted (reversed) dependency tree.
.TP
[\-\-format type]
Specify the output format. Json is the only supported
format. Only some commands support it.
.TP
sync
Synchronizes develop mode dependencies with
the content of the lock file.
.TP
[\-l, \fB\-\-listOnly]\fR
Only lists the packages which are not synced
without actually performing the sync operation.
.TP
setup
Creates `nimble.paths` file containing file
system paths to the dependencies. Also
includes the paths file in the `config.nims`
file to make them available for the compiler.
.TP
shell
Creates a new shell with PATH modified to contain
the bin folders of the dependencies.
.TP
shellenv
Similar to shell command but it returns the script to run in
order to alter the environment. This is intended to be
used in scripts.
.SS "Nimble Options:"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print this help message.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version information.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-accept\fR
Accept all interactive prompts.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-reject\fR
Reject all interactive prompts.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-localdeps\fR
Run in project local dependency mode.
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-global\fR
Run in global dependency mode.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-package\fR
For which package in the dependency tree the
command should be executed. If not provided by
default it applies to the current directory
package. For now, it is used only by the run
action and it is ignored by others.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-tarballs\fR
Enable downloading of packages as tarballs
when working with GitHub repositories.
.TP
\fB\-\-ver\fR
Query remote server for package version
information when searching or listing packages.
.TP
\fB\-\-nimbleDir\fR:dirname
Set the Nimble directory.
.TP
\fB\-\-nim\fR:path
Use specified path for Nim compiler.
.TP
\fB\-\-silent\fR
Hide all Nimble and Nim output.
.TP
\fB\-\-info\fR
Show some informative output.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show extra non\-debugging output.
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Show all output including debug messages.
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
Don't use network.
.TP
\fB\-\-noColor\fR
Don't colorise output.
.TP
\fB\-\-noSslCheck\fR
Don't check SSL certificates.
.TP
\fB\-\-lockFile\fR
Override the lock file name.
.TP
\fB\-\-noLockfile\fR
Ignore the lock file if present.
.TP
\fB\-\-developFile\fR
Specifies the name of the develop file which
to be manipulated. If not present creates it.
.TP
\fB\-\-useSystemNim\fR
Use system nim and ignore nim from the lock
file if any.
.TP
\fB\-\-solver\fR:sat|legacy
Use the SAT solver (default) or the legacy for dependency resolution.
.TP
\fB\-\-requires\fR
Add extra packages to the dependency resolution. Uses the same syntax as the Nimble file. Example: nimble install \fB\-\-requires\fR "pkg1; pkg2 >= 1.2".
.TP
\fB\-\-disableNimBinaries\fR
Disable the use of nim precompiled binaries. Note in some platforms precompiled binaries are not available but the flag can still be used to avoid compile the Nim version once and reuse it.
.TP
\fB\-\-maximumTaggedVersions\fR
Maximum number of tags to check for a package when discovering versions for the SAT solver. 0 means all.
.TP
\fB\-\-parser\fR:declarative|nimvm
Use the declarative parser or the nimvm parser (default).
.TP
\fB\-\-features\fR
Activate features. Only used when using the declarative parser.
.TP
\fB\-\-ignoreSubmodules\fR
Ignore submodules when cloning a repository.
.TP
\fB\-\-legacy\fR
Use the legacy code path (pre nimble 1.0.0)
.TP
\fB\-\-asyncdownloads\fR
Use async for package downloads. (temporary flag)
.SS "For more information read the GitHub readme:"
.IP
https://github.com/nim\-lang/nimble#readme
